# XML choice Codable

Large `if` / `else if` chains and large `switch` / `case` ladders for choice
decode, encode, or seeding ordered items are an anti-pattern. Do not silence
them with `swiftlint:disable cyclomatic_complexity`.

## Bad

```swift
if container.contains(.clip) {
  self = .clip(try container.decode(Clip.self, forKey: .clip))
} else if container.contains(.gap) {
  self = .gap(try container.decode(Gap.self, forKey: .gap))
} // …

if let clips {
  items.append(contentsOf: clips.map(SpineItem.clip))
}
if let gaps {
  items.append(contentsOf: gaps.map(SpineItem.gap))
}
```

## Good

Use `XMLChoiceField` (decode/encode) and `OrderedChoiceItems.appending` (seed
inits), walked with a for-loop:

```swift
for field in Self.fields where container.contains(field.key) {
  self = try field.decode(from: container)
  return
}

self.items = OrderedChoiceItems.appending([
  clips?.map(SpineItem.clip),
  gaps?.map(SpineItem.gap),
])
```

Dispatch choice decode with `container.contains(_:)` only — never try/catch
chaining across cases.
